partio
------------------------------------------
This is the initial source code release of partio a tool we used for particle
reading/writing. It started out as an abstraction for the commonalities in
particle models (i.e. accessing many attributes associated with an index or
entity).

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libGL1-23.3.6-1
  libGLU1-9.0.3-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libglut3-3.4.0-1
  libgtest0-1.18.0-1bl1
  libpartio-devel-1.20.0-1bl1
  libpartio1-1.20.0-1bl1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  pkg-config-3.0.9-1
  python3-3.12.12-1
  zlib0-1.3.2-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libGL-devel-23.3.6-1
  libGLU-devel-9.0.3-1
  libglut-devel-3.4.0-1
  libgtest-devel-1.18.0-1bl1
  ninja-1.13.2-1
  python3-3.12.12-1
  python3-devel-3.12.12-1
  swig-4.5.1-1
  zlib-devel-1.3.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/wdas/partio

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/wdas/partio/archive/refs/tags/v1.20.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack partio-1.20.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./partio-1.20.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/partio-1.20.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/partio-1.20.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libpartio1-1.20.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libpartio-devel-1.20.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/python312-partio-1.20.0-X.tar.xz

